<title>ITALY: Italy Ciampi confirms '97 inflation 2.5 pct target.</title>
<headline>Italy Ciampi confirms '97 inflation 2.5 pct target.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Treasury minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi confirmed the government's target for average inflation at 2.5 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;I confirm that by the end of the year inflation will have fallen to three percent, 2.9 percent or 3 percent it is difficult to be precise, therefore our objective for 1997 stays for 2.5 percent average inflation,&quot; he told the budget commission of Italy's parliamentary lower house.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
